      "title": "asn2wrs: Don't warn about identical duplicate directives in quiet mode",
      "message": "asn2wrs: Don't warn about identical duplicate directives in quiet mode\n\nIf a directive is a duplicate of another, but the parameters (outside of\nthe location in the set of conformation files) are the same, then it's\npedantic to warn about them and we don't need to do so when in quiet\nmode. A common case is when an ASN.1 module's protocol name is given\nmultiple times, with #.MODULE in its own conformation file, but also\nwith the #.MODULE_IMPORT directive in conformance files of other modules\nthat import it.\n\nWe *could* remove the redundant declarations eventually, but we don't\nwant to clutter compared to more significant warnings (which are still\nsometimes intentional.)\n",
